title Caravan restart -- a served child falls mid-conversation, and the standing channel carries the restart home
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, send the finished increment.
think Standfast first. Read crux/REDS.md whole: living rows 80, 83, 84, 85 plus the prose notes. 84 already carries its fix (`.gitignore` line 70 reads `!/crux/`, confirmed on disk), 85 was reopened and closed on metal `20260819.134229` with the witness_claim_check loom standing, 86 released, 81 closed by the crypto count bijection, 83's prevention landed as the living-card ASCII witness. No open agent-closable red stands, so the line is clear for constructive work.
think Council rota, lap 13 of the 27-doc d27 -- `foundations/20260702-165412_the-happy-zone-and-the-thin-edge.md`. It shaped the round directly: gather the pure decisions into a center checked by instant isolated witnesses, press the unruly world into a thin edge. The exit-meaning partition became exactly that center -- 256 codes walked as pure policy with no process spawned -- and the process spawning stayed the thin edge where only real children can tell the truth.
think The last lap's recommend named two candidate cruxes: the unprompted ask, or restart-under-load. Crux-first takes the hardest solvable one, and restart-under-load is it -- fault tolerance is the microkernel's actual value proposition, and Caravan already held the elder exit vocabulary (`supervisor_exit.rye`, `20260707`) waiting to meet the declared world the newer rings built.
think Held a false claim before writing it. My first design said a consumed bell dies with the process, so a restart would need the server to ask again. Reading `roundtrip.hear_from` said otherwise -- hearing reads a counter and never clears it, so the bell is level-standing rather than edge-consumed. Measurement beat memory before a single line was written, and the true claim is the better one: the ring survives the fall.
think That correction gave the ring its real shape. Three things separate cleanly when a child falls -- the bell stands, the memory stands, the progress does not -- and together they name the property: restart is safe when every step is idempotent over declared state. The fall points sit either side of the write, since the write is the only moment a step changes declared state.
think The exit meanings needed care rather than reuse. `supervisor_exit.supervisor_restarts_after_fall` restarts every non-zero, non-8 code, which in this world would restart `NotWired` and `Unheard` -- children answering correctly. So restart.rye consults the outcome vocabulary first: a named outcome is an answer, 8 is a stop, everything else is a fall. The elder module's two constants still hold; what accreted is the world they now read into.
think Compose rather than braid. Five small helpers in serve.rye became pub -- `bell_code`, `reach_code`, `reach_by_name`, `place_message`, `message_stands` -- so restart derives its child steps from the addressed-message vocabulary serve already seated rather than growing a second copy. The serve and roundtrip witnesses both re-ran GREEN afterward, so the accretion carried no regression.
obs GREEN on the first metal pass after two in-lap corrections, then both RED paths proven before the green was trusted. Probe one dropped the outcome vocabulary from meaning_of, and it failed twice over: the pure meaning check caught it before any process ran, and with that check bypassed a correct `NotWired` refusal was restarted four times and declined -- a supervisor spending its whole budget on success. Probe two re-silenced the bells between attempts, and the restarted client answered `Unheard` where `carried` belonged, which is the standing-bell claim stated in reverse.
obs Two corrections taken in-lap, both caught by running rather than reading. The restart-limit check first used a reply verb, so the child answered `Unheard` before the injected fall could land -- a request verb falls before touching anything, which is what the bound actually wanted to measure. And the first loop printed `restart 4/3` at the limit, since it counted a restart it was never going to spend; declining at the boundary reads honestly now.
obs The happy zone paid immediately. `check_meanings` walks all 256 codes with no process at all and asserts the partition is 8 answered, 1 stopped, 247 fallen -- and that instant pure check is precisely what caught probe one first. The thin edge is the five spawned plans, where only real processes can say what survives a real fall.
obs The witness measures from outside the program too: after the after-write plan, each direction of client_a's channel reads exactly 1. A restart that had needed a second ask, or a child that rang twice, would read 2 -- so idempotence is a number on disk rather than a story in the prose.
loom witness=caravan_restart_witness rings=13 plans=5 processes=13 restarts=3 codes_partitioned=256
file caravan/restart.rye the thirteenth ring -- three exit meanings, two fall points, a bounded restart, and what stands through a fall
file caravan/serve.rye five helpers published so restart composes the addressed-message vocabulary rather than copying it
file tools/caravan_restart_witness.rish the witness -- selftest claims read natively, plus bell counts and answer bytes measured from outside
file caravan/README.md the ring table row and the Why a Fall Is Survivable section, docs moving in the same commit as the behavior
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge advanced to thirteen rings and the next crux named
recommend keep-going -- a fall is survivable now, so the next crux is either the unprompted ask (a client ringing a server that has not spoken first, which inverts who starts the conversation) or a restarted child whose capabilities are re-derived from the declaration rather than re-handed by the parent, which is where restart stops trusting the supervisor's memory. No key, no funds, no gate.
